# winoracle (WARP, FL 11_0) x64; the x86 build prints the same lines.
# `undef N` (run separately, one case per process) on WARP:
#   WriteToSubresource / ReadFromSubresource on a DEFAULT CPU-access texture
#   that is not mapped: access violation inside d3d11 (cases 0,1,3,4,6,7,9,10);
#   WriteToSubresource while mapped for READ is gone after the Unmap: the
#   texture keeps its contents (cases 2,5,8,11 print the initial CRC);
#   a DEFAULT texture without CPU access: Map(NULL) E_INVALIDARG, then Write
#   and Read are ignored (cases 12,13); a STAGING texture: Map(NULL)
#   E_INVALIDARG, then Write/Read fault (cases 14,15).
